# Declare Function Types With void

**Rule:** When declaring a variable, parameter, or field whose type is a function that returns nothing, put `void` before `Function`. This avoids linter warnings and makes the intent explicit (a bare `Function(...)` returns `dynamic`).

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
final Function(TransportCode?)? onNavigate;

void doSomething(Function(String) callback) {}
```

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
final void Function(TransportCode?)? onNavigate;

void doSomething(void Function(String) callback) {}
```
